italization and Regulatory Reform Act of 1976.  a"August 3, 1976."  aThis is a publication issued by the United States federal government or produced with federal funds.  aIn scope of the U.S. Government Publishing Office Cataloging and Indexing Program (C&I) and Federal Depository Library Program (FDLP); distribution status could not be determined.  aThis three-part report begins a series of studies mandated by Congress under various sections of the Railroad Revitalization and Regulatory Reform Act of 1976 to determine the best means for rehabilitating and revitalizing the nation's railroads. It is produced in accordance with Section 503(b) and is intended to provide a means of classifying the lines of the Class I railroads of the U.S. to serve a number of purposes under the Act. The prime purpose is to categorize the lines according to reasonable measures of priority so that investments in track can be directed where they will do the most good. Standards used by DOT for priority include traffic density, service to major markets, levels of capacity and national defense. Volume I established a preliminary set of categories and designation for public review, and contains three appendices. Volume II has individual line designations by state and a national map. Additions and corrections are in a separate pamphlet.0 aVol. I: Executive summary -- Introduction -- The development of perliminary standards for classification of rail lines -- The preliminary classificatin of the rail system and designation of rail lines -- Appendices -- Vol. II. Preliminary line designations of the class I railroad network structure. 0aRailroadsxMergerszUnited States. 0aRailroads and statezUnited States. 7aRailroads and state.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01089339 7aRailroadsxMergers.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01089061 7aUnited States.2fast0(OCoLC)fst012041551https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJtxgQXMWqmjMjjwXRHgrq  aC0bGPO  aVEND01b20260529  aHistoric Shelflist Drawer 105