20260908130852.0he |mb   bbca260805s1984    dcua    b    f000 0 eng d  a(OCoLC)1610432177  aGPObengerdacGPOdGPO  an-us---  aGPOO  a0431-K0 aEP 2.8:EL 60 aEP 1.8:EL 2/3  aEPA-440/1-84/091g00aGuidance manual for electroplating and metal finishing pretreatment standards /cprepared by the Effluent Guidelines Division, Office of Water Regulations and Standards and Permits Division, Office of Water Enforcement and Permits. 1aWashington, DC :bU.S. Environmental Protection Agency,c[1984]  a1 volume (various pagings) :billustrations ;c28 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  amicroformbh2rdamedia  amicrofichebhe2rdacarrier  aIn scope of the U.S. Government Publishing Office Cataloging and Indexing Program (C&I) and Federal Depository Library Program (FDLP).  aThis is a publication issued by the United States federal government or produced with federal funds.  a"February 1984."  aAlso distributed to depository libraries in microfiche, Shipping list no.: 94-0990-M.  aMicrofiche.b[Washington, D.C.]cSupt. of Docs., U.S. G.P.O.,d1984.e1 microfiche. 0aElectroplatingxEnvironmental aspectszUnited States. 0aMetalsxFinishingxEnvironmental aspectszUnited States. 7aElectroplatingxEnvironmental aspects.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00907717 7aMetalsxFinishingxEnvironmental aspects.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01018117 7aUnited States.2fast0(OCoLC)fst012041551https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJtxgQXMWqmjMjjwXRHgrq1 aUnited States.bEnvironmental Protection Agency.bOffice of Water Enforcement and Permits.bPermits Division.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8227800708iOnline version:tGuidance manual for electroplating and metal finishing pretreatment standards.w(OCoLC)1043362335  aC0bGPO  aHistoric Shelflist Drawer 298; HSL003;c20260805  aVEND01b2026082603889cam a2200493 i 00147756920260911182437.0m     o  d s      cr |||||||||||260423s2026    dcu     ob   s000 0 eng c  a(OCoLC)1586934463  aMLRbengerdacMLRdOCLCOdGPO  apcc  an-us-mn  aXZL4  a1016-C (online)0 aY 4.G 74/7:C 82/1604aThe Cost of Doing Nothing :bHow Tim Walz and Keith Ellison Fueled Minnesota's Fraud Explosion. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bHouse Committee on Oversight and Government Reform,c2026.  a1 online resource (53 pages)  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  a"March 4, 2026."  a"An Interim Staff Report by the House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform Majority Staff."  a"In December 2025, the House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform launched an investigation into fraud in Minnesota's social services programs that occurred under Governor Tim Walz and Attorney General Keith Ellison's watch. The Committee's investigation has found that senior officials in Minnesota state government, including Governor Walz and Attorney General Ellison, were aware of widespread fraud in federally funded social services programs for years, possessed the legal and procedural authority to stop payments, but repeatedly failed to act. As a result, potentially billions of American taxpayer dollars were allowed to flow to fraudulent actors, while vulnerable populations were harmed and whistleblowers were ignored, sidelined, and retaliated against. While the Committee's investigation remains ongoing, testimony and documents obtained to date establish a consistent pattern: fraud warnings were elevated to senior levels of the Minnesota state government, meaningful corrective action was delayed or avoided, and payments continued long after credible red flags emerged. The Committee's findings raise serious questions about governance and oversight in Minnesota's administration of federal funds. The failure to act decisively in the face of known fraud allowed criminal schemes to flourish and diverted resources away from eligible recipients: the vulnerable populations these programs were intended to serve."--Page 2.  aIn scope of the U.S. Government Publishing Office Cataloging and Indexing Program (C&I) and Federal Depository Library Program (FDLP).  aThis is a publication issued by the United States federal government or produced with federal funds.  aDescription based on online resource; title from PDF cover (viewed April 23, 2026).10aWalz, Tim,d1964-0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n202405350010aEllison, Keith,d1963-0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n201300178010aMinnesota.bGovernor (2019- : Walz)10aMinnesota.bAttorney General.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n81018158 0aLegislative oversightzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075838 0aFraudzMinnesota. 0aExecutive departmentszMinnesota. 0aAdministrative agencieszMinnesota.1 aUnited States.bCongress.bHouse.bCommittee on Oversight and Government Reform,eauthor,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200703483940uhttps://purl.fdlp.gov/GPO/gpo258817704 zAddress at time of PURL creationuhttps://oversight.house.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/The-Cost-of-Doing-Nothing_How-Tim-Walz-and-Keith-Ellison-Fueled-Minnesotas-Fraud-Explosion_3.4.26_FINAL.pdf  aC0bGPO  abc34 20260806b20260806  aBIBCONEWb20260806  aVEND01b2026082602081cam a2200445 i 001477584OCoLC20260904102621.0m     o  d f      cr |||||||||||260807s2026    vaua    o    f000 0 eng d  a(OCoLC)1610531350  aGPObengelocal/GPOepncGPOdOCLCOdOCLCQdGPO  aGPOO  a0624-H (online)0 aI 19.76:2026-1024zI 19,76:2026-102400aEstimating greater sage-grouse population sizes within Oregon :b2017-24. 1aReston, VA :bU.S. Department of the Interior, U.S. Geological Survey,c2026.  a1 online resource (34 pages) :billustrations  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  pillustration0http://rdaregistry.info/termList/IllusContent/10142rdaill1 aOpen-File Report ;v2026-1024  aThis is a publication issued by the United States federal gove